      "content": "That makes sense. We'll look into high-speed oscilloscopes for the time-domain capture.\n\nOne thing that's still bothering me is the \"purposeful\" feeling of it. The disruptions don't just seem random; they seem to happen right when the controller is executing specific logic steps, like transitioning between power modes or initiating a sensor poll. It's as if something knows exactly when to strike to cause a crash without leaving a permanent trace.\n\nCould this be a form of \"logic-based\" interference? Where an attacker isn't just blasting noise, but is instead injecting a very specific, surgically timed signal that exploits a weakness in the controller's communication protocol? How would we even begin to defend against something that feels so... intentional?",
